# Architecture document maintenance

When you change project structure or behavior, update [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) in the **same task**.

## Update the doc when you change

- SQLite schema (`backend/app/db.py`)
- API route groups or major endpoint behavior (`backend/app/main.py`)
- Frontend routes or primary workflows (`frontend/src/App.tsx`, new pages)
- Docker Compose volumes, ports, or env vars
- Core module responsibilities under `backend/app/`
- External dependencies (tesseract, media formats, etc.)

## Do not update for

- Bug fixes, styling, or copy that do not change architecture
- Release version bumps (use CHANGELOG.md instead)
- User-facing how-to steps (use README.md instead)

## How to update

- Edit the relevant existing section; avoid duplicating README or CHANGELOG content.
- Keep mermaid diagrams valid (no spaces in node IDs, no HTML entities in labels).
- If a section no longer applies, remove or rewrite it rather than appending obsolete notes.
